          "Traditionally, AR follow-up has been treated as an ancillary task, often falling to overburdened accounting staff or account executives whose primary focus lies elsewhere. This reactive approach typically results in delayed interventions, where invoices are only chased after they become significantly past due. To combat this inefficiency, a growing paradigm involves the deployment of Virtual Assistant (VA)-managed invoice follow-up protocols. By delegating these specific, process-driven tasks to dedicated remote professionals, organizations can transition from a reactive collection stance to a highly proactive one. This research article explores the operational mechanics and financial impact of utilizing VAs to execute structured AR cadences.",
